From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3had: report variable refresh

The S6E3HAD runs in command mode: it scans out of its own frame memory
and takes a new frame at any TE. Stock's LFD settings, which this driver
sends, also tell it to lower its refresh rate while no frame comes: to
10 Hz at 120HS and 60HS, 12 Hz at 96HS and 48HS, 30 Hz at 60NS. Set
vrr_capable so that compositors can present at the content's rate, and
report 10-120 Hz as the connector's monitor range.

VRR_ENABLED changes nothing on the panel side. Stock has no such state
and always runs LFD with its default range; a frame still goes out on
the next TE either way.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3had.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3had.c
index 09b70de..7cc53ae 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3had.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3had.c
@@ -1493,6 +1493,9 @@ static int s6e3had_get_modes(struct drm_panel *panel, struct drm_connector *conn
 
 	connector->display_info.width_mm = s6e3had_timings[0].mode.width_mm;
 	connector->display_info.height_mm = s6e3had_timings[0].mode.height_mm;
+	/* The LFD range of fhd120hs, the widest of the stock timings */
+	connector->display_info.monitor_range.min_vfreq = 10;
+	connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq = 120;
 	ctx->connector = connector;
 
 	return ARRAY_SIZE(s6e3had_timings);
@@ -1558,6 +1561,12 @@ static int s6e3had_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS | MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
 	ctx->panel.prepare_prev_first = true;
+	/*
+	 * Command mode: the DDI scans out of its own frame memory and takes a
+	 * frame at any TE. Stock's LFD set also tells it to slow its refresh
+	 * while no frame comes, down to 10 Hz at 120HS.
+	 */
+	ctx->panel.vrr_capable = true;
 
 	ctx->panel.backlight = devm_backlight_device_register(dev, dev_name(dev), dev, ctx,
 							       &s6e3had_bl_ops, &props);
